cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "mobius-ramsey: Möbius invariance of the Ramsey property for finite spherical sets (Lean 4)"
version: "1.0.0"
authors:
  - family-names: "Strinz"
    given-names: "Will"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/wstrinz/mobius-ramsey"
abstract: >-
  A Lean 4 proof, with an accompanying note, that the Euclidean Ramsey property of a
  finite set of points on a sphere is invariant under Möbius transformations of the
  sphere (Theorem C), together with corollaries: Möbius images of finite spherical
  sets with algebraic coordinates are Ramsey, and so are the circle families circ(k
  t_i) and circ(t_i + c) for distinct rationals t_i and arbitrary reals k != 0 and
  c. The proof builds on OpenAI's Lean proof of the classification of finite
  Euclidean Ramsey configurations (openai/math, result 172), and trusts it.
  Verification. Every theorem depends only on the axioms propext, Classical.choice
  and Quot.sound; the toolchain's lake comparator (Lean v4.35.0-rc2) accepts the
  proofs against a Mathlib-only statement file with the Lean, NanoDa and con-ron
  kernels, and refuses five negative controls. Not formalized: the classical
  identification of the Lorentz-group maps with the Möbius group, and the reduction
  from an arbitrary sphere to the unit sphere. AI disclosure. The author, Will
  Strinz, is the only human contributor. The proofs, the Lean port, the checks and
  the documentation were produced by AI agents (Claude Opus 5.5 and Claude Sonnet
  5.5, Anthropic, in Claude Code) under his direction; the theorem first appeared in
  a conversation with Claude. The author's read of the hand proof is an owner's
  read, not expert review; no human expert has reviewed this work. See
  DISCLOSURE.md.
  Licence. A mixed tree: this project's own files are under the MIT License; the
  vendored OpenAI Lean files under OAI/ and two PalomarTemplate scripts under
  scripts/ are under the Apache License 2.0. NOTICE lists which file is under
  which licence.
keywords:
  - Euclidean Ramsey theory
  - Möbius transformations
  - Lorentz group
  - spherical configurations
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
  - Mathlib
